"[Box notation for dyn async trait](https://rust-lang.github.io/rust-project-"
"goals/2026/afidt-box.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:168
msgid "Enable dyn dispatch for async traits via `.box` notation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:169
msgid ""
"[Add a `Share` trait](https://rust-lang.github.io/rust-project-goals/2026/"
"ergonomic-rc.html#add-a-share-trait)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:169
msgid ""
"A trait that identifies types where cloning creates an alias to the same "
"underlying value, like `Arc`, `Rc`, and shared references."
msgstr ""

#: src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:170
msgid ""
"[Support `move(...)` expressions in closures](https://rust-lang.github.io/"
"rust-project-goals/2026/ergonomic-rc.html#support-move-expressions-in-"
"closures)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:170
msgid ""
"Precise control over what closures capture and when, eliminating the need "
"for awkward clone-into-temporary patterns."
msgstr ""

#: src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:172
msgid ""
"_People involved: [Takayuki Maeda](https://github.com/TaKO8Ki), [Niko "
"Matsakis](https://github.com/nikomatsakis), [Santiago Pastorino](https://"
"github.com/spastorino)_"
msgstr ""

#: src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:176
msgid ""
"We have a lot of ongoing plans to improve the async Rust experience, but the "
"two most likely to hit stable are [more ergonomic ref-counting](https://rust-"
"lang.github.io/rust-project-goals/2026/ergonomic-rc.html) and [extensions to "
"async fn in traits](https://rust-lang.github.io/rust-project-goals/2026/"
"afidt-box.html)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:178
msgid ""
"The [ergonomic ref-counting](https://rust-lang.github.io/rust-project-"
"goals/2026/ergonomic-rc.html) discussion has gone through [many stages]"
"(https://smallcultfollowing.com/babysteps/series/ergonomic-rc/), but one "
"solid step everyone agrees on is making it (a) more obvious when you are "
"sharing two handles to the same object vs doing a deep clone, via the "
"`Share` trait, and (b) more ergonomic to capture clones into closures and "
"async blocks with `move($expr)` expressions:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:181
msgid "// Today: awkward temporary variables\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:182
msgid "// am I deep cloning or what?\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:186
msgid "// With Share + move expressions: inline and clear\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:190
msgid "//        ---------------- capture a shared handle\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:193
msgid ""
"We also plan to cut a \"practical path\" to support [invoking async fns "
"through `dyn Trait`](https://rust-lang.github.io/rust-project-goals/2026/"
"afidt-box.html). The initial version would be limited to boxed futures but "
"the goal is to be forwards-compatible with the ongoing [in-place "
"initialization](https://rust-lang.github.io/rust-project-goals/2026/in-place-"
"init.html) designs for non-boxed allocation (e.g., stack). The RFC for this "
"hasn't been written yet, and the proposal includes some new syntax, so that "
"could be spicy! Stay tuned."
msgstr ""

#: src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:195
msgid "Try, never, extern types, oh my!"
msgstr ""

#: src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:199 src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:441
#: src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:520 src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:545
#: src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:569 src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:576
#: src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:717 src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:871
#: src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:1023 src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:1170
msgid ""
"[Sized Hierarchy and Scalable Vectors](https://rust-lang.github.io/rust-"
"project-goals/2026/scalable-vectors.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:199
msgid ""
"Over the next year, we will build on the foundational work from 2025 to "
"stabilize the `Sized` trait hierarchy and continue nightly support for "
"scalable vectors:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:200 src/3935-Project-Goals-2026.md:497
